EINVOICING_LIVE=Live-modus ingeschakeld (anders test-/sandbox-modus)
EINVOICING_PDP=Selecteer uw e-factureringsplatform (PA).
EINVOICING_PDP_HELP=Hier worden alleen compatibele E-billing Access Point-platformen weergegeven.
EINVOICING_PDP_HELP2=Depending on the selected platform, the service may be free, have a flat price or be priced per invoice. You should compare them before making your selection.
EINVOICING_PDP_HELP3=Zodra een toegangspunt is geselecteerd, wordt de specifieke configuratie ervan weergegeven.
EINVOICING_ROUTING_ID_HELP=You can enter here a dedicated E-invoice ID for this Access Point. Usually your [SIREN] or [SIREN_suffix] (where suffix can be a SIRET, a free text...).<br>Keep empty to use the default professional ID of your company (for example, the SIREN in France).
EINVOICING_BLOCK_INVOICE_NO_ROUTING_ID=Block invoice generation/sending for third parties without an Electronic Invoicing ID set manually
EINVOICING_BLOCK_INVOICE_NO_ROUTING_ID_HELP=Usually we use an E-invoicing ID auto-generated from third-party information. You can activate this option to disable guessing of the E-invoice ID and prevent creating or sending invoices when a third party has no EXPLICIT Electronic Invoicing ID. <br> If disabled (default, recommended), the E-invoice ID will be guessed if not provided (For example, using the SIREN for French companies).
EINVOICING_AUTO_SEND_ON_GENERATION=Automatisch doorsturen naar de crediteurenadministratie bij factuurvalidatie.
EINVOICING_AUTO_SEND_ON_GENERATION_HELP=Indien ingeschakeld, wordt de e-factuur automatisch naar het toegangspunt verzonden direct nadat deze is gegenereerd (bij factuurvalidatie), zonder dat u op de knop "Verzenden" hoeft te klikken. De factuur wordt niet opnieuw verzonden als deze al is verzonden (geen duplicaat). Vereist dat realtime generatie is ingeschakeld.
EINVOICING_SKIP_B2C=Do not generate e-invoices for private individuals - B2C (invoices will be flagged for eReporting).
EINVOICING_SKIP_B2C_HELP=By default, only invoices generated for non-eligible countries or generated from the Point of Sale modules do not generate e-invoices (they fall in the e-reporting scope). When enabled, e-invoicing is also skipped for some invoices generated from the backoffice if third parties are detected as private individuals (B2C). B2C transactions are out of the e-invoicing scope (they fall under e-reporting). Whether a third party is a company or a private individual is determined by Dolibarr itself (its own detection options), so there is nothing extra to configure here.
EINVOICING_NAME_OF_MODULESOURCE_THAT_ARE_POS=Do not generate e-invoices for invoices generated by the following POS (invoices will be flagged for eReporting).
EINVOICING_NAME_OF_MODULESOURCE_THAT_ARE_POS_HELP=Enter here the list of modules (separated by a comma) that generate invoices and that must be processed as Point Of Sale (POS) so invoices will not be sent individually to the Access Point but aggregated into an eReporting file.
EINVOICING_PARTY_IDENTIFIER_SCHEME=Scheme of the party identifier (BT-29, BT-46)
EINVOICING_PARTY_IDENTIFIER_SCHEME_HELP=Identification scheme the seller and buyer identifiers (BT-29 and BT-46 of EN 16931) are declared under. This is not the electronic address the invoice is routed to (BT-34, BT-49), which always stays on the national directory scheme 0225. The legal registration identifier (BT-30, BT-47) is not affected either: it stays on 0002, the SIREN, as the French specification requires. Outside France, leave the field empty to keep the code the module provides for your country, or enter the ISO 6523 ICD code of the register your professional identifier comes from (0007 Sweden, 0106 Netherlands, 0184 Denmark, 0208 Belgium, 0211 Italy...).
EINVOICING_PARTY_IDENTIFIER_SCHEME_0225=0225 - National directory address, carrying the SIREN (current behavior)
EINVOICING_PARTY_IDENTIFIER_SCHEME_0009=0009 - SIRET, when the third party record holds one
EINVOICING_PARTY_IDENTIFIER_SCHEME_NONE=Do not declare a party identifier
EINVOICING_PARTY_IDENTIFIER_SCHEME_PLACEHOLDER=ISO 6523 ICD code, or empty
EINVOICING_VAT_EXIGIBILITY=BTW-plichtigheid
EINVOICING_VAT_EXIGIBILITY_HELP=Tells when the VAT of an invoice falls due, hence the VAT point date code the document declares, the "VAT on debits" mention it carries and whether a cash-in is reported with the "Cashed in" (212) status. This module does not define that scheme; it reads the VAT mode of the Tax/VAT module setup. Current value, goods / services:
EINVOICING_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB=Maximale bestandsgrootte voor e-facturen (MB)
EINVOICING_MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB_HELP=Indien ingesteld, wordt een niet-blokkerende waarschuwing weergegeven wanneer het gegenereerde e-factuurbestand (XML of PDF/A-3) deze grootte overschrijdt. Laat dit veld leeg of stel het in op 0 om de controle uit te schakelen. Sommige toegangspunten beperken de grootte van geaccepteerde bestanden (bijv. 10 MB voor Chorus Pro).
EINVOICING_TELL_CUSTOMER_PAYMENT_RECEIVED=Informeer de klant wanneer een betaling is ontvangen.
EINVOICING_TELL_CUSTOMER_PAYMENT_RECEIVED_HELP=Send the "Payment received" status (212) to the Access Point when reception of a customer payment is confirmed (payment recorded in the application).
EINVOICING_SEND_PAYMENT_SENT_STATUS=Informeer de leverancier wanneer een factuur is betaald.
EINVOICING_SEND_PAYMENT_SENT_STATUS_HELP=When enabled, the "Payment transmitted" (211) status is sent to the Access Point as soon as a supplier invoice received through the platform is classified as paid in Dolibarr, with the amount paid and its date. It is sent once per invoice. This status is optional in the reform (it is a courtesy to your vendor) and each one costs a flow on your Access Point, hence it is disabled by default.
EINVOICING_SEND_APPROVED_ON_VALIDATION=Informeer de leverancier wanneer een leveranciersfactuur is gevalideerd.
EINVOICING_SEND_APPROVED_ON_VALIDATION_HELP=Disabled by default: the "Approved" (205) status is sent to the Access Point only if enabled. When enabled, it is sent once per invoice, and never on an invoice already answered with "Approved" or "Refused". A failure to send never undoes the validation.
EInvoiceFileSizeExceedsLimit=Het gegenereerde e-factuurbestand (%s MB) overschrijdt de geconfigureerde groottelimiet (%s MB). Uw toegangspunt kan dit bestand weigeren.
EInvoiceFacturxStructureIncomplete=Het gegenereerde Factur-X-bestand %s is geen volledig Factur-X-document (ontbreekt: %s). Het bevat wel de factuurgegevens, maar een lezer of een toegangspunt kan het weigeren.
ErrorEInvoiceCannotEmbedXmlIntoPdf=De XML van de e-factuur kan niet in de PDF worden ingesloten %s: %s. Er is geen Factur-X-bestand gegenereerd.
EInvoiceMassGenerate=Genereer de e-facturen
EInvoiceMassSendToPDP=Stuur de e-facturen naar het toegangspunt.
EInvoiceMassGenerateResult=E-facturen gegenereerd: %s gegenereerd, %s overgeslagen, %s mislukt
EInvoiceMassSendResult=E-facturen verzonden naar het toegangspunt: %s verzonden, %s overgeslagen, %s mislukt
EInvoiceNotGeneratedYetSoNotSent=Er is nog geen e-factuurbestand gegenereerd, er is niets om te verzenden. Genereer het eerst, vanuit de factuur.
EINVOICING_USE_BILLING_CONTACT_AS_BUYER=Gebruik de factuurcontactpersoon als de ontvanger van de e-factuur.
EINVOICING_USE_BILLING_CONTACT_AS_BUYER_HELP=For French invoices only. When enabled, if the invoice has a billing contact (contact of type "Customer invoice contact / BILLING"), this contact is used as the buyer in the generated XML instead of the invoice third party. <br> If the contact belongs to a different third party (e.g. the head office is a separate legal entity), the whole buyer party - name, address, SIREN/SIRET, VAT number and routing ID - is rebuilt from that third party. <br> If the contact belongs to the same third party, only the buyer name/address are overridden while the SIREN, VAT number and routing remain those of the invoice third party. <br> Disabled by default. Note: the XML buyer will then differ from the invoice third party shown in Dolibarr. <br> This option is only about the buyer party: the billing contact itself is always written as the buyer contact (BG-9) of the generated XML, whether the option is enabled or not.
