EINVOICING_AUTO_GENERATION=Synchronisatie van inkoopfacturen (Dolibarr <- PA/PDP)
EINVOICING_EINVOICE_IN_REAL_TIME=Automatic generation of the E-invoice when the invoice is validated.
EINVOICING_EINVOICE_CANCEL_IF_EINVOICE_FAILS=Cancel invoice recording if the automatic generation of the E-invoice fails.
EINVOICING_EINVOICE_CANCEL_IF_EINVOICE_FAILS2=Standaard wordt de factuur aangemaakt, zelfs als het genereren van de e-factuur mislukt. In dat geval kunt u de e-factuur later opnieuw genereren.
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_GENERATION=Automatische generatie van ontbrekende producten
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_GENERATION_HELP=When importing a supplier invoice, if the bought product can't be found in the database, and if there is no default product to use on the supplier card, enabling this option will automatically create missing products during Access Point synchronization, otherwise the synchronization process is stopped until the product has been created manually or a default product for import is set on the vendor card.
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_BARCODE=Give a barcode to the products created at import
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_AUTO_BARCODE_HELP=When a product is created from a received invoice, write the GTIN of the vendor (BT-157) as its barcode, or else take the next code of your barcode numbering module. Disabled by default: the created products get no barcode, so the codes of your numbering are kept for your own products. When your barcode setup requires a barcode on every product, the created products always get the next code of your numbering, regardless of this option.
ErrorEInvoicingBarcodeRequiredOnImport=Your barcode setup requires a barcode on every product, and its numbering module gave none: create the product by hand, or set a mask in the barcode numbering module
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_ROUTING_MIXED=Default product type to use on import when not provided (Mixed invoices)
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_ROUTING_MIXED_HELP=A received invoice states in its billing framework (BT-23) whether it bills goods (B), services (S) or both (M). Its lines with no matching product fall back on the default product of the vendor for B, on its default service for S. However, a mixed invoice does not say what type its lines are, so this option chooses the default type to use. As long as it is empty, the import of a mixed invoice stops with an error when one of its lines needs a type.
ErrorDefaultRoutingMixedUnset=This invoice bills both goods and services (billing framework BT-23 starting with M) without providing information on the type of line (product versus service). Choose in the setup of the module which type of item we must use (product vs service) when no type is provided by the seller.
SetDefaultRoutingMixed=Choose the type of item to use for mixed invoices
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_MATCH_CANONICAL_REF=Match vendor product references whatever their writing
EINVOICING_PRODUCTS_MATCH_CANONICAL_REF_HELP=When a line of an incoming invoice carries a vendor product reference that no supplier price matches exactly, compare it again ignoring separators, case and accents, so that 'A1234-10_42' and 'A1234|10|42' are read as the same reference. This comparison is an approximation and can merge two references that differ only by their separators, so it is disabled by default. The exact comparison is always tried first. When several products of the supplier share the same simplified form, the line is left to the manual product mapping and a warning is written in the log.
EINVOICING_IMPORT_AS_FREE_LINES=Importeer regels zonder product als vrije beschrijvingsregels
EINVOICING_IMPORT_AS_FREE_LINES_HELP=When importing a supplier invoice, if the bought product can't be found in the database, and if there is no default product to use on the supplier card, and automatic product creation is disabled, enabling this option will import the line as a free description line (using the XML label and description) without linking any product. If disabled, the synchronization is stopped until the problem is resolved manually. Enabling this option is a VERY BAD IDEA!
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL=Use a catch-all product for lines with no product
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_HELP=When importing a supplier invoice, if the bought product can't be found in the database and the supplier has no default product or service, the line is linked to the catch-all product chosen below, whatever the supplier. The default product or service of the supplier keeps priority. The lines it catches stay listed on the product mapping screen, so they can be reviewed. Not available with the automatic creation of products.
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_ID=Catch-all product
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_ID_HELP=Product linked to the lines of a received invoice for which no product and no default of the supplier was found. For example a generic "Miscellaneous purchases" product with its own purchase account.
EINVOICING_DEFAULT_PRODUCT_CATCHALL_LOCKED=Enable the option above to choose the product
EINVOICING_THIRDPARTIES_AUTO_GENERATION=Automatische generatie van ontbrekende derden
EINVOICING_THIRDPARTIES_AUTO_GENERATION_HELP=Automatically create missing third parties during Access Point synchronization, otherwise stop the process until the third party has been created manually.
CdarAddressRefusedRecordedRouting=The Access Point does not know %s under the routing identifier recorded for it (%s). Correct that identifier on the third-party card, tab E-invoicing, then send the status again.
CdarAddressRefusedNoRouting=No routing identifier is recorded for %s, so the status was addressed to %s, which the Access Point does not know. Record the routing identifier of that third party on its card, tab E-invoicing, then send the status again.
EINVOICING_DEBUG=Foutopsporing
EINVOICING_DEBUG_MODE=Bewaar alle details van API-aanroepen in de geschiedenis.
EINVOICING_DEBUG_MODE_HELP=Schakel de debugmodus in om alle details van synchronisatieaanroepen vast te leggen voor het oplossen van problemen (uitgebreid). Houd er rekening mee dat synchronisatieaanroepen langer kunnen duren wanneer deze modus is ingeschakeld.
